## Security Considerations
- Validate all parameter updates through governance
- Ensure module account permissions are correctly set
- Validate emission splitting math for overflow/underflow
- Implement proper access controls for keeper methods
- Test edge cases with zero/maximum values

## Performance Considerations
- Emission calculations happen every block - optimize for speed
- Use integer arithmetic where possible to avoid precision loss
- Cache frequently accessed parameters
- Minimize state reads/writes per block

## Backwards Compatibility
- Maintain compatibility with existing mint module queries
- Preserve inflation parameter semantics
- Ensure governance parameter updates work seamlessly
- Support migration from existing mint module state

